<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chepni</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Çepni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chepni are a Turkic tribe of the Oghuz family who settled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> region of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> in the 13th and 14th centuries. They raided and pressed on the Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> and served local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beyliks</a> of the Pontic hinterland. Their descendants live mainly in the provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giresun">Giresun</a>, Trabzon and Ordu in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chepni.jpg" alt="Chepni" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Faigl.ladislav · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cepni.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
